# Arbor code graph (project MCP)

Optional local MCP (gitignored `.cursor/mcp.json` → `arbor.exe` **`bridge`**). Not required to build/ship app. Playbook: [fantasia-arbor](../skills/fantasia-arbor/SKILL.md).

## Use first (when namespace ready)

Call graph / “who uses this” / blast radius / orient in unfamiliar module:

| Need | Tool |
| --- | --- |
| Find symbol | **`search_symbols`** |
| Who calls / what it calls | **`get_callers`** / **`get_callees`** |
| File internals | **`get_file_graph`** |
| Path between two | **`find_path`** / **`get_logic_path`** |
| Change impact (node) | **`analyze_impact`** |
| Uncommitted git ripple | **`get_blast_radius`** |
| Ranked skeleton | **`get_map`** (`exclude_test` default on) |
| Orient | **`get_architecture_overview`**, **`list_entry_points`**, **`explain_symbol`** |

Inspect schema via **`GetDynamicTools`** then **`CallDynamicTool`**. Prefer **project** Arbor namespace; no user-level Arbor duplicate.

## Still Grep / Read

- Exact strings, i18n keys, **`data-test-locator`**, IPC channel names
- Connected Vitest paths ([fantasia-dev-scoped-verify](../skills/fantasia-dev-scoped-verify/SKILL.md) — colocated specs + importer ripgrep)
- MCP **missing**, **error**, or **auth** needed → Grep/Read; do not block the task
- Ranks/entry points can be noisy (tests, stubs). Treat as hints; confirm with Read

## Bug / reuse (with YAGNI)

Before patching one caller: **`get_callers`** on the shared helper. Grep if graph empty or MCP down. [yagni.mdc](yagni.mdc).
